  "Description": "Fresh Start Band (key item, not consumed) resets all six EVs to 0. REBUILT 2026-09-26 on the bag's real use path, replacing the FlipTokuseiIndex/Ability-Capsule design, which could never run for these items: Bag.cro 0x99D4 sends only item 645 to the Ability Capsule flow, so the old 0x099DC/0x0DCBC hooks forced every custom id into the 'change Ability?' prompt instead. Now the item is an ordinary non-645 clone: Use goes 0x977C -> 0x9C50 -> 0xC2F0, where one shared block (bag-item-effects) hooks both ITEM_RCV_RecoverCheck calls (0xC318 use, 0xDDC8 ABLE label), the no-handler branch (0xC358) and the message fallback (0x80DC). Handlers call code.bin directly (ChangeTalentPower / ChangeEffortPower / SetTokuseiIndex recalc stats themselves; nature is written where GetSeikaku reads it and stats refreshed), with the Ultra Moon +8 drift of 0x4A____ functions probed at runtime. Success plays the stock use sound and a message (bag text file 1, lines 159-164, added by this package); no effect shows 'It won't have any effect.' Consumption follows the item's own UseKeep flag.",
